  "physical_meaning": "The full product Green function G_P(x_i, x_j) between separated nodes is smooth. The divergence is an artifact of the sector decomposition: individual AA or BB sectors can diverge even though the total over all sectors (including AB) converges. This means the AA/BB contribution to the inter-node interaction CANNOT be computed as an independent sector sum. It must be combined with source normalization, gauge projection, or a reorganized partial summation that keeps one full factor's Green function unsplit.",
  "consequence_for_coefficient": "The AB sector result (K_adj^AB \u2248 -0.031) is well-defined because both factors involve separated-point evaluation. The AA/BB sector requires a different computational strategy: either (a) keep the scalar factor's coincident sum as a delta-function and extract the regular part after singular subtraction, or (b) reorganize the spectral sum by first summing over the coincident factor analytically (using the factor heat kernel or Green function at the diagonal), then summing over the separated factor. Strategy (b) is the Strategist's suggestion: the coincident scalar sum produces a scalar heat kernel at the diagonal point, which can be handled with zonal derivative identities."
